{"id":"heart-character-of-the-renewed","name":"Heart, Character Of The Renewed","aliases":["Heart"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:heart-character-of-the-renewed"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Heart","text":"According to the Bible, the heart is the centre not only of spiritual activity, but of all the operations of human life. “Heart” and “soul” are often used interchangeably (Deut. 6:5; 26:16; comp. Matt. 22:37; Mark 12:30, 33), but this is not generally the case. The heart is the “home of the personal life,” and hence a man is designated, according to his heart, wise (1 Kings 3:12, etc.), pure (Ps. 24:4; Matt. 5:8, etc.), upright and righteous (Gen. 20:5, 6; Ps. 11:2; 78:72), pious and good (Luke 8:15), etc. In these and such passages the word “soul” could not be substituted for “heart.” The heart is also the seat of the conscience (Rom. 2:15). It is naturally wicked (Gen. 8:21), and hence it contaminates the whole life and character (Matt. 12:34; 15:18; comp. Eccl. 8:11; Ps. 73:7). Hence the heart must be changed, regenerated (Ezek. 36:26; 11:19; Ps. 51:10-14), before a man can willingly …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3820","lemma":"לֵב","xlit":"lêb","gloss":"the heart","kjv":"care for, comfortably, consent, considered","count":27,"share":0.54},{"strong":"H3824","lemma":"לֵבָב","xlit":"lêbâb","gloss":"the heart","kjv":"bethink themselves, breast, comfortably, courage","count":12,"share":0.24},{"strong":"G2588","lemma":"καρδία","xlit":"kardía","gloss":"the heart","kjv":"heart","count":8,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H3559","lemma":"כּוּן","xlit":"kûwn","gloss":"to be erect","kjv":"certain, confirm, direct, faithfulness","count":5,"share":0.1},{"strong":"H5315","lemma":"נֶפֶשׁ","xlit":"nephesh","gloss":"a breathing creature","kjv":"any, appetite, beast, body","count":5,"share":0.1}],"verses":["1Sam.1.13","1Sam.2.1","1Sam.24.5","2Chr.17.6","Ps.9.1","Ps.10.17","Ps.27.3","Ps.27.8","Ps.34.18","Ps.51.17","Ps.57.7","Ps.84.2","Ps.97.11","Ps.1